    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n32729" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ōpĭlĭo</span></b>  and <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ūpĭlĭo</span></b> ,
		ōnis, m.
		for ovilio, from ovis, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a shepherd</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">etiam opilio, qui pascit alienas oves,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. As. 3, 1, 36</span></i>
			.— 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Form upilio,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					E. 10, 19</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Col. 7, 3, 13</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Dig. 32,
				1, 60</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Vulg. Gen. 38,
			12</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A kind of bird</i>, otherwise unknown, <i><span class="en">Fest. p.
				191</span></i> Müll.</div>
